Read legacy Mali gralloc image metadata through its vendor query API.

Prefer the existing standard mapper paths. On older Mali gralloc, load the
HAL through SPHAL and query its immutable format, dimensions, dma-buf, offset,
byte stride, size and layer count. Accept only single-layer RGBA/RGBX/BGRA
with an explicitly unmodified internal format and validated allocation bounds.
Compressed, multi-plane and unknown layouts remain rejected. No imported
contents are modified and no pitch is inferred from the public descriptor.

API definitions: Android device/amlogic/yukawa ddb3cd9,
gralloc/mali_gralloc_private_interface.h and .cpp (Arm/AOSP Apache-2.0).
The x1s vendor library exposes and validates this interface; its metadata was
cross-checked on controlled AHardwareBuffer allocations before this patch.

